-- pending: #54 (two lends in one call)
-- One call that lends two places: a borrowed separator (`&sep`, `imm`) and the output
-- capability (`&mut stdout`, handed back).
--
-- Axes: effects × coeffects × scope: an `imm` demand and a capability in one call.
--
-- Blocked by: the surface. SPEC §14 Open: "A call lends at most one capability with `&mut c`".
-- Each lend is elaborated at the call, as a borrow around it or as a move handed back first;
-- two of them need both hand-backs threaded through one result. `corpus/axes/effects-coeffects.bc`
-- is this program with the capability passed and rebound by name.
--
-- Spelling: today's surface.
--
-- Today: the checker reports a type mismatch at the second lend: the elaboration of the two lends
-- does not line up (`ref output` expected where the separator's borrow is). With the lends in the
-- other order, the elaborator says "a call lends at most one capability with `&`".
--
-- Once it lands: as `corpus/axes/effects-coeffects.bc`. Golden: the line `1,2,3,`, then
-- `i32[44]`, `live 0`.

def emit : !(all 'a < top. imm 'a i32 * (Out * i32) => Out * 1) =
  !thunkv Fun 'a < top. return (thunkv fun (p : imm 'a i32 * (Out * i32)) ->
    let (sep, r) = p;
    let (o, n) = r;
    let (o, _) = put_dec(o, n);
    let s = *sep;
    putb(o, to_u8(s)))

main -> i32 =
  let sep = alloc(44);
  emit(&sep, &mut stdout, 1);
  emit(&sep, &mut stdout, 2);
  emit(&sep, &mut stdout, 3);
  putb(&mut stdout, 10);
  free(sep)
-- now: 31:14: type mismatch: expected `ref output`, but this has type `imm 'io_lb31_3 i32`
